  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224904/assets/7c5e30b2851a8268c5193c2f87e3c6ab77645db4d165d83150fb504ba06ef5c2.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal radius $6$ and vertical radius $5,$ as shown above. Construct a set of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ that traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $H(6,0).$\n\n$x=$ \n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$ \n{{field-2}}$,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).$",
